CVE-2026-27446: Missing authentication/authorization for Core protocol downstream federation connect (CWE-306)

Apache ActiveMQ Artemis did not authenticate or authorize CORE-protocol
FEDERATION_DOWNSTREAM_CONNECT packets, letting an unauthenticated remote
attacker force the broker into an outbound Core downstream federation
connection to an attacker-controlled broker (message injection/exfiltration).

Backport of upstream commit 521e672e4108675806d748158444ce23f9ef76ca
(released in 2.52.0) to 2.40.0. The FEDERATION_DOWNSTREAM_CONNECT handling is
split into a dedicated FederationChannelHandler that, when security is enabled,
rejects unauthenticated connections and connections whose subject lacks a role
listed in the new federationDownstreamAuthorization configuration parameter.

Origin: upstream, https://github.com/apache/activemq-artemis/commit/521e672e4108675806d748158444ce23f9ef76ca
